1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,000
CodexForge tackles 400 Kaggle NeuroGolf ARC tasks.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:08,900
In Kaggle NeuroGolf, each solution is a correct, compact ONNX
computational graph.

3
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:15,600
The principle is simple: use Codex for reasoning; use deterministic
software for orchestration.

4
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:23,100
Repository state enters a deterministic Python control plane that
owns scheduling, locks, retries, timeouts, and logs.

5
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:30,650
It fans tasks out to Codex workers, then verifies builders,
explanations, scores, and ONNX submissions.

6
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:38,300
The repository packages the runner, quota supervisor, dashboard,
prompts, tests, and workspaces.

7
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:45,700
Here, a live campaign selects tasks 12 through 15, with at most two
workers active.

8
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:53,300
Each worker receives exactly one Kaggle NeuroGolf ARC task and an
isolated workspace.

9
00:00:53,550 --> 00:01:01,400
Workers inspect examples and ARC-GEN generators, infer the rule, and
synthesize ONNX graphs.

10
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:10,050
The dashboard turns structured Codex events into readable phases
while retaining raw JSONL logs.

11
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:19,100
Workers can run for hours, so a parent reasoning agent should not
stay active merely to poll them.

12
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:28,300
Deterministic Python handles concurrency, locks, process
supervision, retries, timeouts, cancellation, and resumability.

13
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:37,950
As task 12 completes, its builder, explanation, ONNX submission,
result, and event history become visible.

14
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:46,950
The official scorer rewards correct ONNX programs with lower
combined memory and parameter cost.

15
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:57,350
Every worker tests packaged examples, probes fresh generator cases,
debugs failures, and iterates toward a smaller graph.

16
00:01:57,650 --> 00:02:08,150
Task-local READMEs record validation counts, exhaustive tests, cost,
score, hashes, and the final submission path.

17
00:02:08,450 --> 00:02:17,400
Open worker slots are filled automatically, so queued tasks start
without human coordination.

18
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:27,900
Completed tasks leave durable evidence while other Codex workers
continue reasoning and optimizing in parallel.

19
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:38,750
By now, tasks 12 through 14 are verified, while task 15 continues
testing and optimization.

20
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:45,400
Quota monitoring runs independently from the worker control plane.

21
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:52,400
The legacy view shows why this matters: parallel work otherwise
becomes terminals, logs, and manual status checks.

22
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:59,450
CodexForge makes long-running Codex campaigns observable,
verifiable, and resumable—without a parent agent polling.
